infographic sequence-snake-steps-underline-text
data
  title Napkin math: from 500M users to the scaling axis
  desc Each step derives the next — the binding constraint emerges as concurrent connections, not request rate
  sequences
    - label 500M daily active users
      desc Most keep the app connected, so the system holds hundreds of millions of concurrent long-lived connections
    - label ~100k sockets per gateway
      desc One server holds tens-to-low-hundreds of thousands of idle WebSockets (memory and fd-bound), so you need thousands of gateway servers just to terminate connections
    - label ~250k messages/second
      desc ~40 messages/user/day across 500M users is 2x10^10/day, about 250,000 msg/s average — multiplied at peak
    - label Several TB/day stored
      desc ~20 billion small messages/day at a few hundred bytes each: storage is dominated by count, demanding a write-optimized, sharded store
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
